// A label on a NAMED native signature is validated exactly like one on a declared function.
//
// `math.pow` declares `param_names: &["base", "exp"]`, which is what opts it into named arguments —
// so `zzz:` is not "this callee takes no labels", it is "this callee has no such parameter", and the
// diagnostic can suggest the ones it does have. A signature that declares NO names refuses labels
// instead; both answers are honest, and neither is the old behaviour of dropping the label.
//
// This is the negative half of the native-label surface; `named_arguments_native_bind.noe` pins the
// positive half (binding, reordering, and piping into a named parameter).
// expect: error E0061 at 14:15
// expect: exit 1
use std.math

echo math.pow(zzz: 2.0, exp: 3.0)
